      "writtenOn": "2024-09-13T05:24:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should call the thread.join() somewhere as well? Will it be better off to create a handlerThread and use handler.post() here, and in the tearDown() we do the clean up?\n\n\n```\n    private val handlerThread by lazy {\n        HandlerThread(\"$TAG handler thread\").apply { start() }\n    }\n    private val handler by lazy { Handler(handlerThread.looper) }\n\n\n    @After\n    fun tearDown() {\n        handlerThread.quitSafely()\n        handlerThread.join()\n    } \n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 89,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 89,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "6fb828d4584802e4d6e7afb2e81a1a6bfe876345",
