      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T07:07:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What sort of cleanup do you suggest? Are you concerned about the ThreadLeakMonitor?\n\nThis thread starts, completes the future, and then stops immediately, so it won\u0027t leak.  Also, ThreadLeakMonitor ignores these threads, which are all called something like \"Thread-19\", \"Thread-42\", etc., and which therefore are all groups of one.\n\nFWIW I think using multiple uncoordinated threads here is good because otherwise all queries would always complete in the order they were sent, which is not true on real networks.",
